title: "Rectifiability, finite Hausdorff measure, and compactness for non-minimizing Bernoulli free boundaries, in Lean"
version: "0.4.1"
license: "Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/willmfeldman/bernoulli-rectifiability"
authors:
  - family-names: Feldman
    given-names: "William M."
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of the main results of D. Kriventsov and G. S. Weiss,
  "Rectifiability, finite Hausdorff measure, and compactness for non-minimizing Bernoulli free
  boundaries" (Comm. Pure Appl. Math., 2025): for variational solutions of the Bernoulli free
  boundary problem, the topological free boundary is countably rectifiable with locally finite
  Hausdorff measure, the Laplacian of the solution is identified as an explicit measure on the
  free boundary, and limits of classical solutions are variational solutions. For the functional
  with a Lipschitz coefficient Q, it also proves the identification of χ, the relative closedness
  and density characterization of the set of highest density, the viscosity property off that
  set, and the existence and homogeneity of blow-up limits. It includes a standalone
  formalization of Sperner's inequality for homogeneous harmonic functions.
keywords:
  - Lean
  - Mathlib
  - formalized mathematics
  - free boundary problems
  - Bernoulli problem
  - rectifiability
  - geometric measure theory
  - calculus of variations
